From de0354b9ef245efabf3a024d66c4ac7c8f22d57c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:02:19 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] ASoC: qcom: q6apm: add out-of-band APM SET_CFG

A SET_CFG packet larger than the ADSP glink intents (about 2.2 kB)
cannot be sent in band. Add q6apm_set_cfg_oob(), which, as Qualcomm's
GSL does, copies the parameter records to 4 KiB-aligned pages mapped
on the q6apm-dai device (the one behind the ADSP IOMMU), maps them with
APM_CMD_SHARED_MEM_MAP_REGIONS, sends APM_CMD_SET_CFG by address, checks
the per-record errors, and unmaps. Its commands use a config map token
bit so their answers never touch the PCM map handles.

A buffer whose map or unmap outcome is unknown may still be mapped by
the DSP, and freeing it would hand its IOVA to the next mapping. It is
quarantined per DSP session and released on a later acknowledged
unmap, or when the lpass subsystem restarts; any left at removal are
leaked. The APM and q6apm-dai get suppress_bind_attrs for the same
reason. Out-of-band SET_CFG is unavailable when q6apm-dai memory is
SCM-assigned or the DSP does not echo whole tokens.

